### unsigned-enumerated-zero
# Item 3 (not implemented, conflicts with ASHRAE 135 clauses 20.2.4 and
# 20.2.11): Unsigned and Enumerated values have at least one contents octet,
# so 0 stays 21 00 / 91 00 (the standard's own example is Enumerated 0 ->
# X'91' X'00'), and contents of length 0 are rejected when decoding.
enc_unsigned 0
enc_enum 0
enc_ctx_unsigned 1 0
enc_ctx_enum 1 0
dec_app 2100
dec_app 9100
dec_app 20
dec_app 90
---
OK 2100
OK 9100
OK 1900
OK 1900
OK n=2 u 0
OK n=2 enum 0
ERR
ERR
